    <p>
      <b>Algorithms</b>
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Algebraic block.</li>
      <li>Input 1 is top data, input 2 is condition value, input 3 is bottom data.</li>
      <li>condition supports gt, ne, and ge; unknown values fall back to ge.</li>
      <li>C code generation follows condition; Rust code generation currently treats the condition input as nonzero/zero.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <b>Equation or Rule</b>
    </p>
    <latex>y = \begin{cases} u_1, &amp; \operatorname{condition}(u_2, threshold) \\ u_3, &amp; \mathrm{otherwise} \end{cases}</latex>
    <p>
      <b>Extended Capabilities</b>
    </p>
    <p>This page describes the native runtime behavior observed in the module C++ sources. Declared phases indicate when the simulation engine calls the block.</p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
